<title>UK: Legal and General buys site from UK govt.</title>
<headline>Legal and General buys site from UK govt.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Department of Transport said on Tuesday it had sold its 250-acre research site at Crowthorne in Berkshire to Legal &amp; General Assurance Society Ltd for 18.2 million stg with a clawback provision on the undeveloped part of the site.</p>
<p>Junior minister John Bowis said the deal was a good one for taxpayers. The main tenant is the Transport Research Laboratory, which the government sold to the private sector last year.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom 44-171-542 7767</p>
